PLACEHOLDER FOR docs/assets/demo.gif
=====================================

This file is a marker, not the actual asset. Tracking issue: #8.

WHY THIS EXISTS
---------------
Issue #8 establishes `docs/assets/` as the canonical home for GnomeDoom
documentation media and asks for a fresh hero demo GIF showing the skeleton
cast. The convention work (this directory + its README) has been completed
on branch `docs/issue-8-assets-convention`, but capturing the actual GIF
requires a live GNOME Shell session with the extension installed and the
skeleton characters spawned — something only a human on a real desktop can
do.

WHAT YOU (THE MAINTAINER) NEED TO DO
------------------------------------
1. Install / enable this extension on a GNOME 47+ session.
2. Spawn the full skeleton cast via the panel indicator.
3. Record ~3-8 seconds following the guidance in `docs/assets/README.md`
   ("Suggested demo content" section).
4. Optimise with `gifsicle -O3 --lossy=80 demo.gif -o demo.gif` until the
   file is <= 5 MB.
5. Save the result as `docs/assets/demo.gif` (replacing nothing — this
   placeholder file should be DELETED in the same commit).
6. Issue #2 (README rewrite) will reference it via
   `![demo](docs/assets/demo.gif)`.

Until that GIF is committed, issue #8 cannot be fully closed — only the
convention half is done.
